From: farjanatech <168655490+farjanatech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:20:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] RPi5: publish active HDMI timing and EDID for Windows DOD

Expose the modern Raspberry Pi firmware display-timing and per-display EDID
mailbox tags through the existing firmware protocol. Whenever DisplayDxe
successfully sets a GOP mode, query both display heads, select the active
head whose reported active geometry matches the GOP mode, and publish a
versioned volatile UEFI runtime variable containing the exact firmware timing
and up to four checksum-valid EDID blocks.

The handoff variable is deliberately volatile: it has boot-service and runtime
access but no NON_VOLATILE attribute, so this experiment does not add NVRAM
wear or persistent platform state. No display timing, HDMI register, resource,
fan, SD, Wi-Fi, PCIe, USB or framebuffer programming is changed.
---
 Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DisplayDxe/DisplayDxe.c | 116 +++++++++++++++++++
 Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/RpiFirmwareDxe/RpiFirmwareDxe.c | 120 ++++++++++++++++++++
 Platform/RaspberryPi/Include/IndustryStandard/RpiMbox.h | 2 +
 Platform/RaspberryPi/Include/Protocol/RpiFirmware.h | 44 +++++++
 4 files changed, 282 insertions(+)

